The test simulation command failed because the download URL pointing to https://jquery.com pulls down a raw HTML webpage instead of the plain JavaScript dependency file (.js). Retire.js ignores standard HTML framework markups when looking for direct JavaScript signatures, causing it to return a clean result.
## The Correct Way to Trigger a Test Vulnerability Alert
To properly test the security engine, download an actual outdated script asset from the official jQuery CDN: [1] 
## Step 1: Download the actual script asset file
Execute curl targeting the exact, unminified obsolete jquery-1.12.4.js path: [2] 

curl -O https://code.jquery.com/jquery-1.12.4.js

## Step 2: Run Retire.js on the folder manually
Point your offline scanner at the directory using the local security configuration file:

retire --path . --jsrepo jsrepository.json

